Detect GDK's X11 backend at compile time, not by running a program.

meson.build compiles and *runs* a test program to see whether GDK was built
with X11, which a cross build cannot do ("Can not run test applications in
this cross environment"). The answer is a preprocessor condition, so a
compile check that fails without GDK_WINDOWING_X11 gives the same result.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -217,12 +217,11 @@
 #ifdef GDK_WINDOWING_X11
   return 0;
 #else
-  return 1;
+#error no X11 backend
 #endif
 }
 '''
-result = c_comp.run(code, name : 'GDK has X11 backend', dependencies : gtk_dep)
-use_x11 = result.returncode() == 0
+use_x11 = c_comp.compiles(code, name : 'GDK has X11 backend', dependencies : gtk_dep)
 if use_x11
   common_deps += dependency('x11')
 endif
